  "sort": 400000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you finish a Long Rest, you can inscribe one of the following runes on a melee weapon you are holding, or transfer the rune to a different weapon. Whenever you gain a level, you can replace it with a different rune.</p><p><strong>Blood.</strong> When you inscribe this rune, and whenever you finish a Long Rest while it is inscribed, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Paladin level. While wielding the inscribed weapon, you gain these Temporary Hit Points whenever you reduce an enemy to 0 Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Frost.</strong> While wielding the inscribed weapon, the damage of your weapon attacks, Paladin spells, and Paladin features ignores Resistance to Cold damage. When you make the extra attack of the Light property and hit while wielding it, you deal an extra 1d4 Cold damage.</p><p><strong>Unholy.</strong> While wielding the inscribed weapon, the damage of your weapon attacks, Paladin spells, and Paladin features ignores Resistance to Necrotic damage. If the weapon has the Heavy property, the first creature you hit with it each turn takes extra Necrotic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
